opensync-lab: report the association request IEs (assoc_ies).

OSW reads a station's capabilities from the elements of its (Re)Association
Request: hostapd's STA output and its AP-STA-CONNECTED event are expected to
carry them as assoc_ies=<hex> (osw_hostap.c, osw_drv_nl80211.c). Upstream
hostapd reports neither, so owm treats every station as BTM-incapable
(assoc_req_info.wnm_bss_trans) and its steering can only deauthenticate. Keep
a copy of the elements (from the SSID element on, as OSW parses them) and
report them in both places.

--- a/src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c
+++ b/src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c
@@ -373,6 +373,15 @@ static int hostapd_ctrl_iface_sta_mib(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 		len += os_snprintf(buf + len, buflen - len, "\n");
 	}
 
+	if (sta->assoc_req_ies &&
+	    buflen - len > 11 + 2 * wpabuf_len(sta->assoc_req_ies)) {
+		len += os_snprintf(buf + len, buflen - len, "assoc_ies=");
+		len += wpa_snprintf_hex(buf + len, buflen - len,
+					wpabuf_head_u8(sta->assoc_req_ies),
+					wpabuf_len(sta->assoc_req_ies));
+		len += os_snprintf(buf + len, buflen - len, "\n");
+	}
+
 	if (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_WDS && sta->ifname_wds) {
 		ret = os_snprintf(buf + len, buflen - len,
 				  "wds_sta_ifname=%s\n", sta->ifname_wds);
